      ],
      "source": "https://www.vaco.org/county-connections/visit-stafford-county-and-the-stafford-county-historic-courthouse/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Stafford County was created in 1664 and organized two years later, making it one of Virginia’s oldest counties.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.vaco.org/county-connections/visit-stafford-county-and-the-stafford-county-historic-courthouse/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area served as a stop on the Richmond, Fredericksburg and Potomac Railroad in the 19th century, a line now operated by CSX Transportation.",
